<node id="DIPHOSPHOGLYCOLYLPROLINE (DPGP)">
  <data key="d0">DIPHOSPHOGLYCOLYLPROLINE (DPGP)</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Competitive inhibitor synthesized for the MDD study and relevant to inhibitor targeting of the enzyme binding regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP analogue purchased for nucleotide-related MDD experiments and relevant to nucleotide-binding-region structural interpretation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.65</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_3,a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d6">0.88</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">D283A MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">A substitution mutant of MDD in which Asp283 is replaced by alanine. The figure caption indicates that this mutant has additional ATPγS interactions relative to wild-type MDD.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="RESIDUES 185-191 LOW-DENSITY SEGMENT">
  <data key="d0">RESIDUES 185-191 LOW-DENSITY SEGMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">A sequence segment between residues 185 and 191 that frequently showed poor electron density in the crystallographic maps, preventing complete or accurate modeling in several MDD structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="INCOMPLETE POLYPEPTIDE MODELING">
  <data key="d0">INCOMPLETE POLYPEPTIDE MODELING</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">The crystallographic modeling outcome in which parts of each polypeptide chain could not be fully modeled because of poor electron density, especially around residues 185-191.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.62</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE SITE">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE SITE</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">The ligand-binding cavity of MDD where ordered inhibitor, substrate, and/or nucleotide molecules were modeled. ATPγS-interacting side chains are identified within this pocket. | Catalytic pocket containing MVAPP, ADPBeF3, ligand electron density, and two metal-associated spherical densities in the closed complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.94</data>
  <data key="d7">ACTIVE SITE</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS INTERACTION GEOMETRY">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS INTERACTION GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">The active-site contact arrangement involving the nucleotide analogue ATPγS and nearby MDD side chains, defined using interaction distances of approximately 2.5-3.4 Å.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="WT MDD ATPΓS-INTERACTING SIDE CHAINS">
  <data key="d0">WT MDD ATPΓS-INTERACTING SIDE CHAINS</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Wild-type MDD side chains located within interaction distance of ATPγS in the active site. These residues are marked in the structure-based sequence alignment and define the native nucleotide-contact pattern.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ADDITIONAL ATPΓS INTERACTIONS IN THE D283A MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">ADDITIONAL ATPΓS INTERACTIONS IN THE D283A MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Additional ATPγS contacts annotated for the D283A mutant compared with wild-type MDD, indicating a mutation-associated change in the nucleotide-binding contact network.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.83</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="FMVAPP INHIBITOR CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">FMVAPP INHIBITOR CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">The inhibitor FMVAPP as bound in the S. epidermidis MDD cocrystal structure together with ATPγS. It is modeled in the active site as part of the ligand-bound structural context.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS NUCLEOTIDE ANALOGUE CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS NUCLEOTIDE ANALOGUE CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">The nucleotide analogue ATPγS as bound in the S. epidermidis MDD active site. The structural analysis identifies side chains within 2.5-3.4 Å of ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ORDERED ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND OCCUPANCY">
  <data key="d0">ORDERED ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND OCCUPANCY</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">The observation that unmodeled contiguous electron density corresponded to ordered ligands in the active sites of MDD copies within the asymmetric unit, except for one unoccupied active site in the WT FMVAPP/ATPγS cocrystal.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="SINGLE ACTIVE-SITE OCCUPANCY IN WT FMVAPP/ATPΓS COCRYSTAL">
  <data key="d0">SINGLE ACTIVE-SITE OCCUPANCY IN WT FMVAPP/ATPΓS COCRYSTAL</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">The specific occupancy pattern in the wild-type MDD cocrystal with FMVAPP and ATPγS where only one active site was occupied; the second MDD copy in the asymmetric unit was therefore modeled as apo.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="APO CONFORMATION OF SECOND MDD COPY">
  <data key="d0">APO CONFORMATION OF SECOND MDD COPY</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">The ligand-free conformation assigned to the second MDD copy in the wild-type FMVAPP/ATPγS cocrystal structure because no ligand occupancy was detected in its active site.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="RESIDUE CONSERVATION ACROSS MDD HOMOLOGUES">
  <data key="d0">RESIDUE CONSERVATION ACROSS MDD HOMOLOGUES</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">The conservation pattern observed in a limited structure-based sequence alignment of prokaryotic and eukaryotic MDD proteins, used to contextualize active-site and ATPγS-interacting residues.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="2FO-FC AND FO-FC DIFFERENCE MAPS">
  <data key="d0">2FO-FC AND FO-FC DIFFERENCE MAPS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallographic electron-density maps calculated after coordinate and isotropic atomic displacement factor refinement. They were used for model improvement, ligand placement, and assessment of poorly modeled regions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
