  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">The 2.19 Å X-ray cocrystal structure of S. epidermidis MDD bound to inhibitor FMVAPP and nucleotide analogue ATPγS, providing structural evidence for active-site ligand binding and ATPγS contacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="LIMITED STRUCTURE-BASED SEQUENCE ALIGNMENT">
  <data key="d0">LIMITED STRUCTURE-BASED SEQUENCE ALIGNMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">A ClustalW-generated alignment of prokaryotic and eukaryotic MDD proteins, colored by residue conservation and annotated with WT ATPγS-interacting side chains and additional D283A mutant ATPγS interactions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="CONSTRAINED GROUP OCCUPANCY REFINEMENT">
  <data key="d0">CONSTRAINED GROUP OCCUPANCY REFINEMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">The refinement procedure used for complexed MDD structures to estimate the fraction of ligand bound at each active site independently.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
