  <data key="d0">SPACE GROUP P212121 CRYSTAL FORM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystal form of MDD associated with eight copies of MDD per asymmetric unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.48</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD ACTIVE SITE CLEFT">
  <data key="d0">MDD ACTIVE SITE CLEFT</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Ligand-binding cleft in MDD where contiguous Fo-Fc electron density supported modeling of one FMVAPP molecule and one ATPγS molecule; corresponds to the investigated ATP-binding site.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS-BOUND FMVAPP TERNARY MDD STATE">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS-BOUND FMVAPP TERNARY MDD STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Ligand-bound crystallographic state of S. epidermidis MDD containing both FMVAPP and the nucleotide analogue ATPγS in a single active site cleft.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="FMVAPP">
  <data key="d0">FMVAPP</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhibitor/substrate-analogue ligand co-crystallized with ATPγS in the MDD active site; modeled with final occupancy near 78%. | Substrate analog, 6-fluoromevalonate 5-diphosphate, used in PMDsc structural analysis to assess residue proximity to the phosphate group.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_5</data>
