  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conformation in the S192A ternary structure where the P-loop remains locked in the apo-like state despite the presence of both substrate and nucleotide analogues.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS TRIPHOSPHORYL LOCALIZATION">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS TRIPHOSPHORYL LOCALIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Positioning of the ATPγS triphosphoryl group in the active site; this localization is adversely affected by loss of Ser192.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="S192A APO-SUPERPOSITION EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">S192A APO-SUPERPOSITION EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural comparison showing that all 330 C-alpha atoms of S192A ternary MDD align with apo-S192A MDD within 5.0 Å, with an rmsd of 0.49 Å.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="FO-FC LIGAND-DENSITY EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">FO-FC LIGAND-DENSITY EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Difference electron-density maps showing contiguous, well-defined density in both S192A MDD active sites, supporting modeling of FMVAPP and ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="P-LOOP REGION OF MDD">
  <data key="d0">P-LOOP REGION OF MDD</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP-binding loop in MDD containing residues including Ala101, Gly103, and Leu104; its conformation is central to ATPγS triphosphoryl positioning and active-site closure.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="P-LOOP APO CONFORMATION">
  <data key="d0">P-LOOP APO CONFORMATION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactive/open-like conformation retained by the P-loop in the S192A ternary structure despite the presence of FMVAPP and ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ATPΓS TRIPHOSPHORYL-GROUP LOCALIZATION">
  <data key="d0">ATPΓS TRIPHOSPHORYL-GROUP LOCALIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Observed positioning of the ATPγS triphosphoryl group; adversely affected when the P-loop remains locked in the apo conformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="S192A MDD TERNARY COMPLEX WITH FMVAPP AND ATPΓS">
  <data key="d0">S192A MDD TERNARY COMPLEX WITH FMVAPP AND ATPΓS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Cocrystal structure of S. epidermidis S192A MDD bound to FMVAPP and ATPγS; shows lack of P-loop conformational change and preserves apo/FM VAPP-bound space-group behavior. | 2.60 Å cocrystal structure of S. epidermidis D283A MDD bound to MVAPP and ATPγS; crystals belonged to space group P212121 and contained eight copies in the asymmetric unit.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d7">D283A MDD TERNARY COMPLEX WITH MVAPP AND ATPΓS</data>
</node>
<node id="APO-S192A MDD STRUCTURAL ALIGNMENT">
  <data key="d0">APO-S192A MDD STRUCTURAL ALIGNMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Superposition evidence showing all 330 Cα atoms align within 5.0 Å with an rmsd of 0.49 Å between the S192A ternary structure and apo-S192A MDD.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A KCAT">
  <data key="d0">D283A KCAT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic rate for S. cerevisiae D283A MDD, reported as kcat = 1.64 × 10^-5 s^-1, representing about a 10-fold decrease.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A KM FOR MVAPP">
  <data key="d0">D283A KM FOR MVAPP</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Michaelis constant for MVAPP in S. cerevisiae D283A MDD, reported as 397 μM, representing about a 3-fold increase.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A KM FOR ATP NOT DIRECTLY DETERMINED">
  <data key="d0">D283A KM FOR ATP NOT DIRECTLY DETERMINED</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP KM for D283A MDD could not be directly measured because the mutant had very low activity at subsaturating ATP and low intrinsic ATPase activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A FO-FC LIGAND DENSITY">
  <data key="d0">D283A FO-FC LIGAND DENSITY</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Contiguous high-quality Fo−Fc difference density in each active site of the D283A ternary crystal, supporting high-occupancy modeling of MVAPP and ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAPP AND ATPΓS HIGH-OCCUPANCY MODELING">
  <data key="d0">MVAPP AND ATPΓS HIGH-OCCUPANCY MODELING</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Both MVAPP and ATPγS were modeled at greater than 88% occupancy in all eight D283A active sites before final refinement.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="D283A REFINEMENT STATISTICS">
  <data key="d0">D283A REFINEMENT STATISTICS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Final crystallographic refinement of the D283A ternary complex gave Rwork = 19.9% and Rfree = 25.1%, supporting the structural model.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="Β9-HELIX 5 CONNECTING LOOP">
  <data key="d0">Β9-HELIX 5 CONNECTING LOOP</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Loop comprising residues 182–192 that moves into a position enabling conserved Lys188 to contact the γ-phosphoryl group of ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="LYS188">
  <data key="d0">LYS188</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conserved active-site lysine positioned by the β9-helix 5 loop to interact with the γ-phosphoryl group of ATPγS.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
