  <data key="d0">MDD ACTIVE-SITE CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase active site examined in ternary cocrystal structures with nucleotide analogue ATPγS and either inhibitor FMVAPP or substrate MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="GHMP KINASE SUPERFAMILY CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">GHMP KINASE SUPERFAMILY CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Protein-family context for MDD; GHMP kinases catalyze sequential transfer of the ATP γ-phosphoryl group to an enzyme-specific acceptor.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="SEQUENTIAL Γ-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER REACTION">
  <data key="d0">SEQUENTIAL Γ-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER REACTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Canonical GHMP kinase reaction in which the γ-phosphoryl group of ATP is transferred to an acceptor, yielding ADP and a phosphorylated product.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="ACCEPTOR-FIRST SUBSTRATE-BINDING ORDER IN MDD">
  <data key="d0">ACCEPTOR-FIRST SUBSTRATE-BINDING ORDER IN MDD</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Binding-order feature noted for MDD, where acceptor binding occurs before ATP binding, unlike some other GHMP kinase members.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.62</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
<node id="P-LOOP">
  <data key="d0">P-LOOP</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-site motif whose movement contributes to formation of the nucleotide-bound MDD active-site funnel. | A conserved phosphate-binding sequence motif cited as common in ATP- and GTP-binding proteins. In this extraction it is treated as a motif-level determinant of nucleotide engagement rather than as a complete binding reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9,a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_12,a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_14</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d7">P-LOOP</data>
</node>
<node id="Β-SHEET 9–HELIX 5 LOOP">
  <data key="d0">Β-SHEET 9–HELIX 5 LOOP</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-site loop whose position changes in MDD mutants and strongly affects the size and occlusion of the active-site funnel.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</node>
