  <data key="d2">Major loop displacement triggered by MVAPP binding that modulates the ATP-binding pocket and prepares the enzyme for ATP recognition.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP-BINDING POCKET">
  <data key="d0">ATP-BINDING POCKET</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Binding-site geometry whose configuration is altered after MVAPP binding to favor subsequent ATP accommodation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d6">0.88</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP-ENGAGED CLOSED-LOOP STATE">
  <data key="d0">ATP-ENGAGED CLOSED-LOOP STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conformational state after ATP binding in which the phosphate-binding loop closes over the active site to arrange MVAPP and ATP in a catalytically favored configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="TWO-MG2+ CATALYTIC CONFIGURATION">
  <data key="d0">TWO-MG2+ CATALYTIC CONFIGURATION</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-site metal-binding arrangement in which positioned substrates chelate two Mg2+ ions required for the phosphoryl-transfer and decarboxylation steps.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE-SITE ENTRANCE CLOSURE">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE-SITE ENTRANCE CLOSURE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Later conformational closure of the active-site entrance that brings a conserved lysine into the correct position for catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CONSERVED CATALYTIC LYSINE">
  <data key="d0">CONSERVED CATALYTIC LYSINE</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conserved lysine residue positioned by active-site closure to trigger dissociative transfer of ATP γ-phosphate to MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="DISSOCIATIVE PHOSPHORYL TRANSFER">
  <data key="d0">DISSOCIATIVE PHOSPHORYL TRANSFER</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic step in which the γ-phosphate of ATP is transferred to MVAPP through a dissociative phosphoryl-transfer mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-PRODUCING DECARBOXYLATION">
  <data key="d0">IPP-PRODUCING DECARBOXYLATION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Final reaction step following phosphorylation in which the MVAPP-derived intermediate undergoes decarboxylation to produce isopentenyl diphosphate.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="SEQUENTIAL INDUCED-FIT TRAJECTORY">
  <data key="d0">SEQUENTIAL INDUCED-FIT TRAJECTORY</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall ordered conformational pathway in which MVAPP binding, ATP binding, loop closure, Mg2+ chelation, and lysine positioning collectively drive catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF ENZYME SYSTEM">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF ENZYME SYSTEM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase from Enterococcus faecalis V583, a VRE strain, studied structurally, functionally, and biophysically as a bacterial MDD target.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.96</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD FAMILY MVAPP-BINDING SITE">
  <data key="d0">MDD FAMILY MVAPP-BINDING SITE</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Highly conserved substrate-binding pocket for mevalonate diphosphate across MDD proteins, including bacterial and human MDDs; conservation creates selectivity challenges for inhibitor design.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE-SITE CONFORMATIONAL REARRANGEMENT">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE-SITE CONFORMATIONAL REARRANGEMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Programmed structural changes in and around the MDD active site during substrate binding and catalysis, involving loop and helix movements.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="BETA10-ALPHA4 LOOP">
  <data key="d0">BETA10-ALPHA4 LOOP</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Mobile loop near the active site of MDDEF implicated in substrate-binding-associated conformational rearrangements.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ALPHA1 HELIX">
  <data key="d0">ALPHA1 HELIX</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary structural helix in MDDEF that participates in conformational rearrangements around the active site. | Secondary structural helix adjacent to the beta10-alpha4 loop, involved in active-site conformational rearrangement.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.78</data>
  <data key="d7">ALPHA4 HELIX</data>
</node>
<node id="K187">
  <data key="d0">K187</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conserved lysine residue in MDDEF identified as having a critical catalytic role.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_7,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_8,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_9,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_11,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_21</data>
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CATALYTIC ASP RESIDUE">
  <data key="d0">CATALYTIC ASP RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Conserved aspartic acid residue, corresponding to D282 in Enterococcus faecalis MDD, D283 in Staphylococcus epidermidis MDD, and D281 in Sulfolobus solfataricus MDD; implicated in dephosphorylation/decarboxylation and possibly phosphoryl transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ORDERED MVAPP BINDING">
  <data key="d0">ORDERED MVAPP BINDING</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">First substrate-binding step in the sequential ordered bi-substrate mechanism of MDDs, where mevalonate diphosphate binds before ATP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP BINDING">
  <data key="d0">ATP BINDING</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Second substrate-binding step in the ordered MDD mechanism, occurring after MVAPP binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.83</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_17</data>
  <data key="d6">0.88</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="GAMMA-PHOSPHATE TRANSFER TO MVAPP">
  <data key="d0">GAMMA-PHOSPHATE TRANSFER TO MVAPP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic step in which the gamma-phosphate group of ATP is transferred to MVAPP to generate the 3-prime-phosphate-MVAPP intermediate.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="3-PRIME-PHOSPHATE-MVAPP INTERMEDIATE">
  <data key="d0">3-PRIME-PHOSPHATE-MVAPP INTERMEDIATE</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorylated reaction intermediate generated after ATP-dependent phosphoryl transfer to MVAPP. | Phosphorylated MVAPP intermediate generated after ATP-dependent phosphorylation of the MVAPP 3′-hydroxyl group.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.89</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.94</data>
  <data key="d7">3′-PHOSPHATE-MVAPP INTERMEDIATE</data>
</node>
<node id="DEPHOSPHORYLATION AND DECARBOXYLATION">
  <data key="d0">DEPHOSPHORYLATION AND DECARBOXYLATION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Downstream catalytic conversion of the 3-prime-phosphate-MVAPP intermediate leading to formation of isopentenyl diphosphate.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_14</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d0">IPP PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Formation of isopentenyl diphosphate as the product of MDD-catalyzed dephosphorylation and decarboxylation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.79</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MAGNESIUM-ION CATALYTIC REQUIREMENT">
  <data key="d0">MAGNESIUM-ION CATALYTIC REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">MDD catalysis requires magnesium ions, although prior published MDD structures did not identify bound metal ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="D281T/D281V PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER DEFICIENCY">
  <data key="d0">D281T/D281V PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER DEFICIENCY</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Reduced phosphoryl transfer efficiency observed for D281T and D281V mutants of Sulfolobus solfataricus MDD compared with wild type, indicating involvement of the conserved Asp in phosphoryl transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="FMVAPP INHIBITOR SELECTIVITY LIMITATION">
  <data key="d0">FMVAPP INHIBITOR SELECTIVITY LIMITATION</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">6-fluoromevalonate diphosphate inhibits MDD but binds the highly conserved MVAPP-binding site, including in human MDD, raising potential side-effect concerns.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDSS MUTAGENESIS EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">MDDSS MUTAGENESIS EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutagenesis studies on Sulfolobus solfataricus MDD supporting a role for the catalytic Asp in dephosphorylation/decarboxylation rather than only 3-prime-OH deprotonation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="STRUCTURE-BASED SPECIFICITY REQUIREMENT">
  <data key="d0">STRUCTURE-BASED SPECIFICITY REQUIREMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Need for MDD inhibitor development with bacterial sensitivity and human-target specificity to avoid side effects during treatment of bacterial infections.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD_EF CATALYTIC MECHANISM">
  <data key="d0">MDD_EF CATALYTIC MECHANISM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall mechanistic context for Enterococcus faecalis mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase, inferred from ligand-bound crystal structures representing different reaction states. | Overall mechanistic context for the MDDEF enzyme, covering substrate binding, active-site assembly, phosphate-transfer chemistry, dephosphorylation, decarboxylation, and product formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.95</data>
  <data key="d7">MDDEF CATALYTIC MECHANISM</data>
</node>
