  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CLOSED MVAPP-ADP-SO4^2−-CO2+ MDD_EF STATE">
  <data key="d0">CLOSED MVAPP-ADP-SO4^2−-CO2+ MDD_EF STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed conformation of MDD_EF captured with MVAPP, ADP, sulfate, and Co2+, used to generate a nearly full-length structural model.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="LIGAND-SOAKED ACTIVE MDD_EF CRYSTALS">
  <data key="d0">LIGAND-SOAKED ACTIVE MDD_EF CRYSTALS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystals grown in high ammonium sulfate, buffer-exchanged into PEG3350, and soaked with substrates or cofactors, enabling activity and trapping of reaction states in the crystal.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD_EF CRYSTAL-STRUCTURE SERIES ACROSS REACTION STEPS">
  <data key="d0">MDD_EF CRYSTAL-STRUCTURE SERIES ACROSS REACTION STEPS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Set of apo, substrate-bound, open, and closed MDD_EF crystal structures used to analyze conformational changes during the enzyme mechanism.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="TWO-LAYER ΑΒ SANDWICH ARCHITECTURE">
  <data key="d0">TWO-LAYER ΑΒ SANDWICH ARCHITECTURE</data>
  <data key="d1">DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall MDD_EF fold composed of α and β secondary-structure elements, similar to previously published MDD structures.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="DRUG DEVELOPMENT AGAINST PATHOGENIC BACTERIAL MDD PROTEINS">
  <data key="d0">DRUG DEVELOPMENT AGAINST PATHOGENIC BACTERIAL MDD PROTEINS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Application context in which detailed understanding of the MDD enzyme mechanism may support development of drugs targeting MDD proteins from drug-resistant pathogenic bacteria.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.6</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Enterococcus faecalis mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase variant/form discussed in the structural analysis. | The mevalonate diphosphate decarboxylase construct designated MDD_EF in the excerpt. It is the enzyme component of the reported ligand-, nucleotide-, sulfate-, and metal-bound crystallographic states.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.88</data>
  <data key="d7">MDD_EF</data>
</node>
<node id="APO-MDDEF STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d0">APO-MDDEF STRUCTURE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">X-ray structural evidence for apo MDDEF, also described as MDDEF-SO42−, in which the phosphate-binding loop and β10-α4 loop could not be determined.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF-MVAPP STRUCTURE">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF-MVAPP STRUCTURE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">MVAPP-bound structural model of MDDEF in which MVAPP and the β10-α4 loop are clearly visible.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="PHOSPHATE-BINDING LOOP (97-104)">
  <data key="d0">PHOSPHATE-BINDING LOOP (97-104)</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional loop near the active-site entrance that is unresolved in apo MDDEF but becomes positioned close to the β10-α4 loop in the closed complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="Β10-Α4 LOOP (183-190)">
  <data key="d0">Β10-Α4 LOOP (183-190)</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Loop preceding helix α4; unresolved in apo MDDEF, visible in the MVAPP-bound structure, and brought near the phosphate-binding loop in the closed active-site conformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="HELIX Α4">
  <data key="d0">HELIX Α4</data>
  <data key="d1">DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d2">Local helical structural element following the β10-α4 loop; residues S191 and R192 on this helix interact with MVAPP pyrophosphate and help stabilize the preceding loop.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_6,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_8,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="S191">
  <data key="d0">S191</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Serine residue on helix α4 that forms bonding interactions with the pyrophosphate of MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_8,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_9,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_11</data>
  <data key="d6">0.94</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="R192">
  <data key="d0">R192</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Arginine residue on helix α4 that interacts with the pyrophosphate of MVAPP and contributes to stabilization of the β10-α4 loop.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="S106">
  <data key="d0">S106</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Serine residue whose γ-OH oxygen coordinates one of the metal-associated spherical densities in the closed MDDEF complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.73</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_7,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d6">0.91</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAPP PYROPHOSPHATE">
  <data key="d0">MVAPP PYROPHOSPHATE</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Pyrophosphate moiety of MVAPP that forms interactions with S191 and R192 on helix α4 and contributes to loop stabilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ADPBEF3">
  <data key="d0">ADPBEF3</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Bound nucleotide/ATP-analogue component in the closed MDDEF-MVAPP-ADPBeF3-Mg2+ structure; contributes oxygen ligands to one metal-binding site and BeF3− fluorine to another.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MG2+">
  <data key="d0">MG2+</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Magnesium ion required for the MDD reaction and assigned to the two metal-associated densities in the closed MDDEF complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_17</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="WATER">
  <data key="d0">WATER</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Coordinating water molecules that contribute oxygen ligands to the metal-binding geometry in the closed MDDEF active site.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="DYNAMIC OR DISORDERED LOOP STATE">
  <data key="d0">DYNAMIC OR DISORDERED LOOP STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Inferred apo-state regime in which the phosphate-binding loop and β10-α4 loop are mobile or disordered, consistent with their absence from the determined apo structure and lack of crystal-packing contacts.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="STABILIZED Β10-Α4 LOOP CONFIGURATION">
  <data key="d0">STABILIZED Β10-Α4 LOOP CONFIGURATION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Defined β10-α4 loop conformation observed in the MVAPP-bound structure; proposed to be stabilized through MVAPP-pyrophosphate interactions with helix α4 residues S191 and R192.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CLOSED CONFORMATION OF MDDEF">
  <data key="d0">CLOSED CONFORMATION OF MDDEF</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed active-site state in which the β10-α4 loop and phosphate-binding loop move close together around the active-site entrance. | Open conformational state of MDDEF in which ATP binding is inferred to be initially weak before active-site rearrangement.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.94</data>
  <data key="d7">OPEN CONFORMATION OF MDDEF</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE SITE ENTRANCE">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE SITE ENTRANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Entrance region of the catalytic pocket that becomes enclosed by the phosphate-binding loop and β10-α4 loop in the closed MDDEF complex. | Entrance to the MDDEF catalytic pocket that is closed by the β10-α4 loop and phosphate-binding loop before catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.89</data>
  <data key="d7">ACTIVE-SITE ENTRANCE</data>
</node>
<node id="METAL-BINDING SITE 1">
  <data key="d0">METAL-BINDING SITE 1</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">First active-site metal-binding site, assigned to Mg2+, surrounded by oxygen atoms from MVAPP, ADPBeF3, S106 γ-OH, and water. | Second active-site metal-binding site, assigned to Mg2+, coordinated by oxygen atoms from water and MVAPP plus a fluorine atom from BeF3−.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.84</data>
  <data key="d7">METAL-BINDING SITE 2</data>
</node>
<node id="TWO METAL-BINDING SITES">
  <data key="d0">TWO METAL-BINDING SITES</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Pair of active-site metal-binding sites inferred from extra spherical densities and confirmed by anomalous cobalt signal; proposed to bind the magnesium ions required for the MDD reaction. | Metal-binding geometry formed by the ATP phosphate tail, S106, and the pyrophosphate of MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_6</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.91</data>
  <data key="d7">FIRST METAL-BINDING SITE</data>
</node>
<node id="TWO EXTRA SPHERICAL DENSITIES">
  <data key="d0">TWO EXTRA SPHERICAL DENSITIES</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Electron-density observation in the closed MDDEF complex showing two spherical densities not belonging to MVAPP or ADPBeF3, interpreted as metal ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="LIGAND DENSITIES IN THE ACTIVE SITE">
  <data key="d0">LIGAND DENSITIES IN THE ACTIVE SITE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Clear active-site electron density allowing bound MVAPP, ADPBeF3, and additional spherical densities to be distinguished.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="DISTINCT ANOMALOUS SIGNAL OF COBALT IONS">
  <data key="d0">DISTINCT ANOMALOUS SIGNAL OF COBALT IONS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Anomalous diffraction evidence from cobalt ions that confirmed the positions of the two metal-binding sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="NO CRYSTAL-PACKING CONTACTS">
  <data key="d0">NO CRYSTAL-PACKING CONTACTS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Observation that the apo-MDDEF phosphate-binding and β10-α4 loop regions lack stabilizing crystal-packing contacts, supporting loop disorder or dynamics.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.77</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="FIRST STEP IN THE MDD REACTION">
  <data key="d0">FIRST STEP IN THE MDD REACTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Initial mechanistic step proposed to be enabled when MVAPP binding stabilizes the β10-α4 loop in a defined configuration.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.81</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD REACTION">
  <data key="d0">MDD REACTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall catalytic reaction performed by MDD, requiring magnesium ions and involving active-site closure around MVAPP and nucleotide-like ligands.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF CATALYTIC DOMAIN">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF CATALYTIC DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d1">DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic MDD construct analyzed in multiple ligand-bound structural states.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND-BINDING POCKET">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND-BINDING POCKET</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Active-site pocket containing MVAPP and ATP-analog ligands; its accessibility and geometry differ between open and closed conformations.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF–MVAPP SUBSTRATE-BOUND CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF–MVAPP SUBSTRATE-BOUND CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural context containing MDDEF bound to MVAPP alone, used as a reference for ligand-binding-site organization.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="OPEN MDDEF–MVAPP–AMPPCP–MG2+ STATE">
  <data key="d0">OPEN MDDEF–MVAPP–AMPPCP–MG2+ STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP-analog-bound MDDEF state in which the active site remains solvent-accessible and the donor-acceptor distance is too long for efficient phosphoryl transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CLOSED MDDEF–MVAPP–ADPBEF3–MG2+ STATE">
  <data key="d0">CLOSED MDDEF–MVAPP–ADPBEF3–MG2+ STATE</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed MDDEF state containing MVAPP, ADPBeF3, and Mg2+, interpreted as a pre-phosphoryl-transfer conformation. | Closed catalytic-state mimic in which the β10-α4 loop covers the active site and K187 extends into the pocket to contact S191 and ADPBeF3.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.96</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.96</data>
  <data key="d7">CLOSED MDDEF-MVAPP-ADPBEF3-MG2+ STATE</data>
</node>
<node id="ADPBEF3 Γ-PHOSPHORYL MIMIC CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">ADPBEF3 Γ-PHOSPHORYL MIMIC CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">ATP-analog context in which BeF3− mimics the γ-phosphoryl group of ATP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="IN-LINE PRE-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER GEOMETRY">
  <data key="d0">IN-LINE PRE-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Geometry in the closed ADPBeF3 complex where BeF3 lies between ADP Oβ and the MVAPP 3′-oxygen with an Oβ–Be–3′O angle of about 178°, consistent with in-line phosphoryl transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.97</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="PRE-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER STEP">
  <data key="d0">PRE-PHOSPHORYL-TRANSFER STEP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Reaction state immediately before phosphoryl transfer, represented by the closed MDDEF–MVAPP–ADPBeF3–Mg2+ complex. | Enzymatic transfer of the γ-phosphoryl group to MVAPP; favored by short, in-line donor-acceptor geometry and disfavored in the open AMPPCP-bound state.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.95</data>
  <data key="d7">PHOSPHORYL TRANSFER STEP</data>
</node>
<node id="EARLIER ATP-BINDING STEP">
  <data key="d0">EARLIER ATP-BINDING STEP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Earlier state upon ATP binding represented by the open MDDEF–MVAPP–AMPPCP–Mg2+ complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="OPEN-STATE SOLVENT ACCESSIBILITY">
  <data key="d0">OPEN-STATE SOLVENT ACCESSIBILITY</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">The active site in the AMPPCP-bound open state remains accessible to solvent.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CLOSED-STATE BULK-WATER EXCLUSION">
  <data key="d0">CLOSED-STATE BULK-WATER EXCLUSION</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed conformation restricts bulk water diffusion into the active site, proposed to avoid wasteful phosphoryl transfer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="OPEN-STATE LONG DONOR-ACCEPTOR DISTANCE">
  <data key="d0">OPEN-STATE LONG DONOR-ACCEPTOR DISTANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">In the open AMPPCP-bound state, the MVAPP 3′-oxygen to AMPPCP Pγ distance is 6.1 Å, substantially longer than the 3.7 Å MVAPP 3′-oxygen to Be distance in the ADPBeF3 complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="AMPPCP WEAK-BINDING SELECTIVITY PROFILE">
  <data key="d0">AMPPCP WEAK-BINDING SELECTIVITY PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">AMPPCP shows about 70% occupancy relative to ADPBeF3 in the closed structure, fewer MDDEF contacts, and implies weak initial ATP/analog affinity for the open conformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="AMPPCP INHIBITION CONSTANT GREATER THAN 1 MM">
  <data key="d0">AMPPCP INHIBITION CONSTANT GREATER THAN 1 MM</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Large KI value for AMPPCP from prior chicken MDD kinetic studies, supporting weak binding of ATP analogs in the open conformation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="SA LIGAND-OMIT MAPS AT 3Σ">
  <data key="d0">SA LIGAND-OMIT MAPS AT 3Σ</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Simulated-annealing ligand-omit electron-density maps contoured at 3σ for MVAPP and nucleotide ligands in MDDEF complexes. | Simulated-annealing ligand-omit electron-density map contoured at 3σ, showing well-defined active-site ligands and two spherical densities.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.82</data>
  <data key="d7">SA-LIGAND-OMIT MAP AT 3Σ</data>
</node>
<node id="MDDEF–MVAPP–ADP–SO4–CO2+ CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">MDDEF–MVAPP–ADP–SO4–CO2+ CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Bound complex containing MDDEF, MVAPP, ADP, sulfate, and cobalt ion, referenced as a structure described in a later section.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="COBALT ANOMALOUS SIGNAL">
  <data key="d0">COBALT ANOMALOUS SIGNAL</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Distinct anomalous signal confirming cobalt ions in the MDDEF–MVAPP–ADP–SO4–Co2+ complex.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="WEAK ATP BINDING AFFINITY IN OPEN MDDEF">
  <data key="d0">WEAK ATP BINDING AFFINITY IN OPEN MDDEF</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Qualitative binding-affinity observation indicating that ATP has weak initial affinity for the open conformation of MDDEF.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE SITE REARRANGEMENT">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE SITE REARRANGEMENT</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Proposed structural reorganization of the MDDEF active site required to accommodate ATP or related ligands after weak initial binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="SUBSTRATE ACCOMMODATION">
  <data key="d0">SUBSTRATE ACCOMMODATION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Mechanistic step in which the substrate becomes properly positioned in the MDDEF active site after conformational or local active-site rearrangement.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CLOSED MDDEF-LIGAND CONFORMATION">
  <data key="d0">CLOSED MDDEF-LIGAND CONFORMATION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Closed ligand-bound state of MDDEF in which active-site loops, ligands, and two metal-binding positions are ordered and structurally resolved.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MDD ENZYMATIC REACTION">
  <data key="d0">MDD ENZYMATIC REACTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic reaction context in which two metal-binding sites are proposed to form during MDDEF catalysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
