  <data key="d0">METAL COORDINATION GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Coordination environment formed by surrounding atoms around the two spherical densities, used to infer that the densities correspond to bound metal ions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND-BINDING REGION">
  <data key="d0">ACTIVE-SITE LIGAND-BINDING REGION</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">MDDEF active-site region containing MVAPP, ADP, SO42− or ADPBeF3, ordered loop elements, and the two metal-binding positions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="COBALT SUBSTITUTION FOR MAGNESIUM">
  <data key="d0">COBALT SUBSTITUTION FOR MAGNESIUM</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Cofactor-substitution profile in which cobalt acts as an alternative cofactor for MDDEF catalysis and enables anomalous crystallographic identification of metal sites.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="COBALT-SUBSTITUTED BUFFER CONDITIONS">
  <data key="d0">COBALT-SUBSTITUTED BUFFER CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental buffer condition in which cobalt replaces magnesium during ligand-bound MDDEF crystallization and enzymatic assays.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MAGNESIUM-CONTAINING CONDITIONS">
  <data key="d0">MAGNESIUM-CONTAINING CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference condition containing magnesium, used for comparison with cobalt-supported MDDEF activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.73</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="LIGAND-BOUND MDDEF CRYSTALS">
  <data key="d0">LIGAND-BOUND MDDEF CRYSTALS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallization context for MDDEF bound to ligands under cobalt-substituted buffer conditions, prepared to test whether two metal-binding sites form.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="VMAX WITH COBALT">
  <data key="d0">VMAX WITH COBALT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Maximum MDDEF reaction velocity measured under cobalt-substituted conditions: 9.5 ± 0.3 μMol min−1 mg−1; approximately 70% of the value observed with magnesium.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="KM FOR MGATP WITH COBALT">
  <data key="d0">KM FOR MGATP WITH COBALT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Michaelis constant for MgATP measured under cobalt-substituted conditions: 188 ± 13 μM. | Michaelis constant for MVAPP measured under cobalt-substituted conditions: 39.3 ± 4.0 μM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
  <data key="d6">0.84</data>
  <data key="d7">KM FOR MVAPP WITH COBALT</data>
</node>
<node id="VMAX UNDER MAGNESIUM">
  <data key="d0">VMAX UNDER MAGNESIUM</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Reference maximum velocity for MDDEF under magnesium-containing conditions, used to show that cobalt-supported Vmax is reduced to about 70%.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="PYRUVATE KINASE CONTROL RATE WITH COBALT">
  <data key="d0">PYRUVATE KINASE CONTROL RATE WITH COBALT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Control rate for pyruvate kinase in the coupled assay under cobalt conditions: 85.4 ± 1.6 μMol min−1 mg−1, demonstrating that reduced MDDEF activity is not due to impaired coupling enzyme activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="MAGNESIUM ELECTRON-DENSITY AMBIGUITY">
  <data key="d0">MAGNESIUM ELECTRON-DENSITY AMBIGUITY</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Limitation that magnesium lacks a readily detectable anomalous signal and its electron density can be difficult to distinguish from water, motivating cobalt-substitution experiments.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
