</node>
<node id="LYSINE 187">
  <data key="d0">LYSINE 187</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">The native lysine residue at position 187 of MDD that is replaced by alanine in the K187A mutant. No specific catalytic, binding, or structural role for this residue is stated in the excerpt.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_20</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="WILD-TYPE MDD PROTEIN">
  <data key="d0">WILD-TYPE MDD PROTEIN</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">The unmutated MDD protein used as a reference comparator for the K187A mutant in enzymology, thermodynamic, and crystallization studies. The source text appears to contain a formatting artifact around the phrase 'wild-type MDD proteins.'</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_20,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_21</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="X-RAY DATA COLLECTION">
  <data key="d0">X-RAY DATA COLLECTION</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Crystallographic diffraction data collection used to support determination of MDD X-ray crystal structures. The excerpt acknowledges assistance with X-ray data collection and use of synchrotron beamlines.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_20</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="CRYSTALLIZATION">
  <data key="d0">CRYSTALLIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">The experimental crystallization workflow applied to purified K187A mutant and wild-type MDD proteins as part of structural characterization.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_20,701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_21</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="THERMODYNAMIC CHARACTERIZATION">
  <data key="d0">THERMODYNAMIC CHARACTERIZATION</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental assessment of thermodynamic properties of the purified MDD protein forms. In this excerpt, this is linked to ITC experiments but no numerical thermodynamic results are reported.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.66</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_20</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
