  <data key="d0">THERMODYNAMICS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermodynamic characterization performed on purified wild-type and K187A MDD protein samples. The text specifically mentions ITC experiments as part of this evidence base.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.58</data>
  <data key="d4">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe_chunk_21</data>
  <data key="d5">701d8434-7f71-5da9-bb94-e869d94e65fe</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-BYPASS MEVALONATE PATHWAYS">
  <data key="d0">IPP-BYPASS MEVALONATE PATHWAYS</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Engineered mevalonate-derived pathways for C5 alcohol production that bypass isopentenyl diphosphate (IPP). These pathways use promiscuous enzyme activities to decouple production from native IPP regulation, reduce energetic requirements, and avoid IPP-related toxicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">1.0</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="ORIGINAL MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d0">ORIGINAL MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">The previously engineered heterologous mevalonate pathway in E. coli, described as a 7-gene route for isopentenol production. It intersects native isoprenoid metabolism at IPP and was optimized to achieve over 50% theoretical yield.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="NATIVE MEP PATHWAY">
  <data key="d0">NATIVE MEP PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">The native methylerythritol 4-phosphate pathway in E. coli, also called the non-mevalonate or DXP pathway. It naturally supplies isoprenoid precursors and intersects the heterologous MVA pathway at IPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-DEPENDENT MVA-MEP COUPLING">
  <data key="d0">IPP-DEPENDENT MVA-MEP COUPLING</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">The regulatory and metabolic coupling created because the MVA and MEP pathways converge at isopentenyl diphosphate, the direct precursor to isoprenoid-derived C5 alcohols and longer-chain terpenes.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="PROMISCUOUS PMD ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d0">PROMISCUOUS PMD ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Noncanonical catalytic activity of phosphomevalonate decarboxylase used in the IPP-bypass MVA pathway. The text identifies PMD activity as the primary determinant of bypass pathway performance.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="PROMISCUOUS APHA PHOSPHATASE ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d0">PROMISCUOUS APHA PHOSPHATASE ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Promiscuous phosphatase activity of the E. coli endogenous enzyme AphA used together with PMD to construct IPP-bypass mevalonate routes for C5 alcohol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="PMD MUTANTS">
  <data key="d0">PMD MUTANTS</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Engineered sequence variants of phosphomevalonate decarboxylase designed to improve PMD activity in the bypass pathway. These variants were reported to increase production titers in mutant strains.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="PMD ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d0">PMD ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic activity of phosphomevalonate decarboxylase in the bypass pathway. The study states that bypass pathway performance was primarily determined by this activity. | Mevalonate kinase activity, described as potentially inhibited by GPP and FPP accumulation, thereby reducing downstream MVA flux.</data>
  <data key="d3">1.0</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d7">MK ACTIVITY</data>
</node>
<node id="BYPASS PATHWAY PERFORMANCE">
  <data key="d0">BYPASS PATHWAY PERFORMANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Overall production output and functional behavior of the engineered IPP-bypass mevalonate pathway. It is mainly governed by PMD activity and is reported to be less affected by reduced aeration than the original MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="ISOPENTENOL TITER INCREASES">
  <data key="d0">ISOPENTENOL TITER INCREASES</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Measured increases in isopentenol production titers observed in strains carrying improved PMD mutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="OVER 50 PERCENT THEORETICAL YIELD">
  <data key="d0">OVER 50 PERCENT THEORETICAL YIELD</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Reported production efficiency achieved after optimization of the MVA-based C5 alcohol pathway in E. coli.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="REDUCED ENERGETIC REQUIREMENTS">
  <data key="d0">REDUCED ENERGETIC REQUIREMENTS</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Energetic advantage attributed to the IPP-bypass MVA pathways relative to the original IPP-forming route.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-RELATED TOXICITY AVOIDANCE">
  <data key="d0">IPP-RELATED TOXICITY AVOIDANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Benefit of the IPP-bypass pathways in which production is described as free from toxicity associated with IPP accumulation or IPP-linked metabolism.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="DECOUPLING FROM NATIVE CELLULAR REGULATION">
  <data key="d0">DECOUPLING FROM NATIVE CELLULAR REGULATION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Desired regulatory state in which the engineered MVA pathway is separated from endogenous E. coli isoprenoid regulation by avoiding the shared IPP node.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="REDUCED AERATION RATE">
  <data key="d0">REDUCED AERATION RATE</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Cultivation condition used to compare the original MVA pathway and the IPP-bypass pathway. The bypass pathway was reported to be less negatively affected under this condition.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="BYPASS AERATION ROBUSTNESS">
  <data key="d0">BYPASS AERATION ROBUSTNESS</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Observed robustness of the IPP-bypass pathway under reduced aeration, reflected by the claim that reduced aeration has less impact on the bypass route than on the original MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</node>
<node id="ENGINEERED E COLI HOST">
  <data key="d0">ENGINEERED E COLI HOST</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">The bacterial host context in which the MVA and IPP-bypass pathways were constructed and evaluated for C5 alcohol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_0</data>
  <data key="d5">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
