<node id="CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d0">CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">The mevalonate-based isopentenol production route in Escherichia coli that proceeds through IPP before hydrolysis to isopentenol. It is described as engineering-limited by high ATP demand and IPP-associated toxicity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d0">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">An alternative MVA-derived isopentenol production route designed to bypass IPP dependency. The pathway uses reactions catalyzed by AtoB, HMGS, HMGR, MK, and PMD and includes promiscuous PMD-mediated conversion of MVAP to IP. | Metabolic production context in which DH1 strains expressing M212Q, R74S, or I145A PMDsc mutants produced 600–800 mg/L isopentenol compared with 475.1 mg/L for WT.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.95</data>
  <data key="d7">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d0">ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Generation of one molecule of IPP through the conventional MVA pathway consumes three ATP molecules, creating a substantial energetic burden.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d0">IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrolysis of the diphosphate group of IPP in the conventional MVA-based isopentenol production route, which wastes ATP previously invested in IPP formation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION">
  <data key="d0">IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">A toxic or inhibitory cellular state proposed to occur when IPP accumulates in Escherichia coli, leading to growth inhibition and possible stress responses.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="OPTIMAL INTRACELLULAR IPP LEVEL">
  <data key="d0">OPTIMAL INTRACELLULAR IPP LEVEL</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">The balanced IPP concentration needed to support isopentenol production while minimizing growth inhibition caused by excessive IPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION TO IP">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION TO IP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">A promiscuous reaction catalyzed by heterologously expressed Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphomevalonate decarboxylase, in which mevalonate phosphate is decarboxylated to form isopentenyl phosphate. | Canonical PMDsc reaction using mevalonate-5-diphosphate as the native substrate; this reaction has much higher catalytic activity than the promiscuous MVAP reaction.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d6">1.0</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d7">PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAPP DECARBOXYLATION</data>
</node>
<node id="ATOB-HMGS-HMGR-MK-PMD REACTION SEQUENCE">
  <data key="d0">ATOB-HMGS-HMGR-MK-PMD REACTION SEQUENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">The five-reaction sequence shown as the solid-arrow IPP-bypass route from acetyl-CoA-derived intermediates through mevalonate phosphate toward isopentenyl phosphate and isopentenol.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMK-PMD-NUDB REACTIONS OF THE ORIGINAL MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d0">PMK-PMD-NUDB REACTIONS OF THE ORIGINAL MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">The three dotted-arrow reactions included in the original MVA pathway, involving PMK, PMD, and NudB, which proceed through phosphorylated isoprenoid intermediates including IPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP-BYPASS SCREENING PLATFORM">
  <data key="d0">IPP-BYPASS SCREENING PLATFORM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">A pathway-screening design that contains IP kinase and IPP isomerase in addition to the five reactions of the IPP-bypass isopentenol pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
