</node>
<node id="ENDOGENOUS PHOSPHATASE HYDROLYSIS OF IP TO ISOPENTENOL">
  <data key="d0">ENDOGENOUS PHOSPHATASE HYDROLYSIS OF IP TO ISOPENTENOL</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Hydrolysis of isopentenyl phosphate to isopentenol by endogenous phosphatases in E. coli.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ARCHAEAL IPK PHOSPHORYLATION OF IP TO IPP">
  <data key="d0">ARCHAEAL IPK PHOSPHORYLATION OF IP TO IPP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphorylation of isopentenyl phosphate to isopentenyl pyrophosphate by heterologously expressed archaeal isopentenyl phosphate kinase.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IPP AND DMAPP FORMATION FOR E. COLI GROWTH">
  <data key="d0">IPP AND DMAPP FORMATION FOR E. COLI GROWTH</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Formation of the essential isoprenoid precursors IPP and DMAPP required to support E. coli growth when the endogenous MEP pathway is blocked.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="GROWTH-LINKED PMD SCREENING PLATFORM">
  <data key="d0">GROWTH-LINKED PMD SCREENING PLATFORM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Selection system in which E. coli growth rate is coupled to PMDsc-mediated MVAP decarboxylation, enabling screening of PMD variants with improved MVAP activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">1.0</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="FOSMIDOMYCIN INHIBITION OF THE MEP PATHWAY">
  <data key="d0">FOSMIDOMYCIN INHIBITION OF THE MEP PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Use of fosmidomycin to inhibit 1-deoxy-D-xylulose 5-phosphate reductoisomerase in the endogenous E. coli MEP pathway, blocking native production of IPP and DMAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="AERATION-LIMITED ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">AERATION-LIMITED ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Production condition under which the IPP-bypass MVA pathway was reported to make isopentenol production more robust than the native MVA pathway by reducing ATP consumption.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.66</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMD VARIANT LIBRARIES">
  <data key="d0">PMD VARIANT LIBRARIES</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Libraries of mutated PMD sequences evaluated in the growth-linked screening platform to identify variants with improved activity toward MVAP and enhanced isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IMPROVED PMD VARIANTS FOR MVAP ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d0">IMPROVED PMD VARIANTS FOR MVAP ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Selected PMD mutants identified from variant libraries that improve isopentenol production through increased functional activity in the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="LOW PMDSC ACTIVITY BOTTLENECK">
  <data key="d0">LOW PMDSC ACTIVITY BOTTLENECK</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional limitation of the IPP-bypass isopentenol pathway caused by weak PMDsc activity toward MVAP, restricting isopentenol titer and productivity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.94</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="DH1 FOSMIDOMYCIN SENSITIVITY">
  <data key="d0">DH1 FOSMIDOMYCIN SENSITIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">E. coli DH1 was more susceptible to fosmidomycin than other tested engineering strains and showed no growth at 10 µM fosmidomycin.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.62</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="KANG ET AL. 2016 EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">KANG ET AL. 2016 EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior study cited for development of the IPP-bypass MVA pathway, reduction of IPP toxicity, improved robustness under aeration-limited conditions, and reported PMDsc activity toward MVAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="KREPKIY AND MIZIORKO 2004 EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">KREPKIY AND MIZIORKO 2004 EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Prior study cited for kinetic characterization of PMDsc activity toward the native substrate MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.58</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_2</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="E. COLI DH1 FOSMIDOMYCIN-SENSITIVE SCREENING HOST">
  <data key="d0">E. COLI DH1 FOSMIDOMYCIN-SENSITIVE SCREENING HOST</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">E. coli DH1 was the most fosmidomycin-sensitive strain among DH1, BL21, and BW25113, showing no growth at 10 µM fosmidomycin and rapid OD600 decline at higher concentrations; it was selected as the host for screening PMD mutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="FOSMIDOMYCIN SELECTION PRESSURE">
  <data key="d0">FOSMIDOMYCIN SELECTION PRESSURE</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Antibiotic selection condition used to inhibit growth unless the heterologous IPP-bypass MVA pathway restores IPP production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAP DECARBOXYLATION BY PMDSC">
  <data key="d0">MVAP DECARBOXYLATION BY PMDSC</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">The phosphomevalonate decarboxylase reaction converting MVAP into IP within the IPP-bypass MVA pathway; this step is the activity being screened.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.98</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IP PHOSPHORYLATION TO IPP">
  <data key="d0">IP PHOSPHORYLATION TO IPP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Kinase-mediated phosphorylation of isopentenol phosphate or IP to produce IPP, allowing restoration of growth under fosmidomycin selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="WILD TYPE PMDSC">
  <data key="d0">WILD TYPE PMDSC</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Wild type Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphomevalonate decarboxylase expressed in DH1 as the baseline enzyme for MVAP decarboxylation activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC-S208E INACTIVE MUTATION">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC-S208E INACTIVE MUTATION</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Inactive PMDsc mutation used as a negative control; co-expression with IP kinases did not permit DH1 growth under fosmidomycin selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC-R74H MUTATION">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC-R74H MUTATION</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc variant associated with faster DH1 growth than wild type under sensitive expression conditions, indicating improved MVAP decarboxylation-linked screening output.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC-K22M MUTATION">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC-K22M MUTATION</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc variant associated with decreased DH1 growth relative to wild type under sensitive expression conditions, indicating reduced MVAP decarboxylation-linked screening output.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ECIPK">
  <data key="d0">ECIPK</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">E. coli IspE kinase with reported activity toward IP; in this screening context it showed weaker growth recovery than archaeal IP kinases.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MTIPK">
  <data key="d0">MTIPK</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Methanothermobacter thermautotrophicus IP kinase; expression enabled DH1 growth recovery under fosmidomycin and produced a shorter lag phase than TaIPK.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="TAIPK">
  <data key="d0">TAIPK</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Thermoplasma acidophilum IP kinase; expression enabled DH1 growth recovery under fosmidomycin, suggesting higher effective IP kinase activity than EcIPK.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="GROWTH RECOVERY UNDER FOSMIDOMYCIN">
  <data key="d0">GROWTH RECOVERY UNDER FOSMIDOMYCIN</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Experimental observation that DH1 growth resumed when active PMDsc and effective IP kinases, particularly MtIPK or TaIPK, were expressed in the IPP-bypass pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="NO GROWTH WITH INACTIVE PMDSC-S208E">
  <data key="d0">NO GROWTH WITH INACTIVE PMDSC-S208E</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Observation that DH1 strains expressing EcIPK, MtIPK, or TaIPK failed to grow when co-expressing inactive PMDsc-S208E, supporting dependence on MVAP decarboxylation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.89</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ATC INDUCTION CONCENTRATION">
  <data key="d0">ATC INDUCTION CONCENTRATION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Anhydrotetracycline inducer concentration used to regulate PMDsc expression, including 10 nM and 100 nM conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="DH1 GROWTH RATE">
  <data key="d0">DH1 GROWTH RATE</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Cellular growth-rate readout used as a proxy for MVAP decarboxylation activity; at high PMDsc expression, active variants K22M, R74H, and wild type showed similar growth rates around 0.83 ± 0.01 h^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.87</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAP DECARBOXYLATION ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d0">MVAP DECARBOXYLATION ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional activity of PMDsc variants inferred from DH1 growth behavior under fosmidomycin selection; higher activity yields faster growth under sensitive screening conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="OPTICAL DENSITY DECREASE AFTER FOSMIDOMYCIN EXPOSURE">
  <data key="d0">OPTICAL DENSITY DECREASE AFTER FOSMIDOMYCIN EXPOSURE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Fast reduction in OD600 after approximately two hours of fosmidomycin exposure in DH1, indicating accelerated cell death at higher fosmidomycin concentrations.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ABSENCE OF ADAPTIVE FOSMIDOMYCIN RESISTANCE">
  <data key="d0">ABSENCE OF ADAPTIVE FOSMIDOMYCIN RESISTANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">No fosmidomycin resistance was observed under screening-platform and growth-recovery conditions, supporting that growth recovery came from the engineered pathway rather than resistance mutations.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_3</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE TARGETED RESIDUES">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE TARGETED RESIDUES</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Set of PMDsc residues selected for codon saturation mutagenesis based on active-site alignment and prior kinetic evidence: Tyr19, Lys22, Arg74, Ile145, Ser208, Thr209, and Met212.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="TYR19">
  <data key="d0">TYR19</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue corresponding to Tyr18 in PMDse; likely positioned near the native substrate MVAPP pyrophosphate-binding region.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d6">0.82</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="LYS22">
  <data key="d0">LYS22</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue corresponding to Lys21 in PMDse; likely interacts with the pyrophosphate group of the native substrate MVAPP. The K22M variant retained active-growth behavior under high inducer conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d6">0.82</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ARG74">
  <data key="d0">ARG74</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue selected based on prior kinetic evidence; substitutions at this position, including R74H and R74S, are implicated in increased decarboxylase activity and improved screening enrichment.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d6">0.95</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ILE145">
  <data key="d0">ILE145</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue selected from prior kinetic evidence; I145F increased decarboxylation kcat for multiple substrates, and I145A improved isopentenol production in the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="SER208">
  <data key="d0">SER208</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue corresponding to Ser192 in PMDse; its hydroxyl side chain is positioned to form hydrogen bonds with α-phosphate groups of ATP and MVAPP in a homologous ternary-complex model.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="THR209">
  <data key="d0">THR209</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue corresponding to Arg193 in PMDse; proposed to provide second-sphere support for active-site residues that directly interact with substrates.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.68</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d6">0.82</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MET212">
  <data key="d0">MET212</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc residue corresponding to Met196 in PMDse; proposed to provide second-sphere structural support. The M212Q mutation significantly improved isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_12</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE POCKET MODEL">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE POCKET MODEL</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Structural model inferred by aligning PMDsc structure 1FI4 with homologous PMDse, indicating conserved active-site features for ATP and MVAPP binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAPP PYROPHOSPHATE-BINDING INTERACTION">
  <data key="d0">MVAPP PYROPHOSPHATE-BINDING INTERACTION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Substrate-recognition step in which conserved residues such as Tyr19 and Lys22 are proposed to interact with the pyrophosphate group of native substrate MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP/MVAPP Α-PHOSPHATE HYDROGEN BONDING">
  <data key="d0">ATP/MVAPP Α-PHOSPHATE HYDROGEN BONDING</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate-binding interaction modeled from PMDse in which Ser208 is positioned to form hydrogen bonds with α-phosphate moieties of ATP and MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC DECARBOXYLATION KCAT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC DECARBOXYLATION KCAT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Catalytic turnover parameter for PMDsc decarboxylation activity; prior data showed variants such as R74H and I145F increased kcat for multiple substrates including 3-hydroxy-3-methylbutyrate and MVAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC KCAT/KM-LINKED GROWTH READOUT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC KCAT/KM-LINKED GROWTH READOUT</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Apparent growth-linked proxy for PMDsc catalytic efficiency used by the screening platform; similar growth rates under high expression reduce the ability to distinguish active variants by relative catalytic activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMD EXPRESSION REGULATION CONTEXT">
  <data key="d0">PMD EXPRESSION REGULATION CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Expression-level condition controlled by inducer concentration; the text indicates PMD expression must be tightly regulated so selection pressure reflects relative catalytic activity of PMDsc mutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="HIGH ATC INDUCER CONDITION">
  <data key="d0">HIGH ATC INDUCER CONDITION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Condition using 100 nM aTc, a 10-fold higher inducer concentration, which increased PMD variant expression and caused DH1 strains expressing active PMDsc K22M, R74H, and WT to show similar growth rates.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="E. COLI DH1 PMDSC SCREENING PLATFORM">
  <data key="d0">E. COLI DH1 PMDSC SCREENING PLATFORM</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth-based selection platform in E. coli DH1 used to enrich PMDsc mutants with increased catalytic activity under fosmidomycin selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="FOSMIDOMYCIN COMPETITIVE-GROWTH SELECTION">
  <data key="d0">FOSMIDOMYCIN COMPETITIVE-GROWTH SELECTION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Mixed-culture selection condition using 10 μM fosmidomycin, in which DH1 strains expressing PMDsc WT, K22M, and R74H competed during serial regrowth.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74H COMPETITIVE DOMINANCE">
  <data key="d0">R74H COMPETITIVE DOMINANCE</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Observed enrichment profile in which DH1 expressing PMDsc-R74H became the dominant strain after multiple dilutions of a mixed culture, indicating selection for higher-activity PMDsc variants.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="CODON SATURATION MUTAGENESIS SCREEN">
  <data key="d0">CODON SATURATION MUTAGENESIS SCREEN</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Library-screening approach applied to rationally targeted PMDsc residues to identify substitutions that improve growth-linked activity and pathway output.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="M212Q/R74S/I145A IMPROVED-PRODUCTION PROFILE">
  <data key="d0">M212Q/R74S/I145A IMPROVED-PRODUCTION PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Selected PMDsc mutation profile from saturation libraries; M212Q, R74S, and I145A significantly increased isopentenol production through the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="SEQUENCING ENRICHMENT EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">SEQUENCING ENRICHMENT EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Sequencing data from mixed DH1 cultures showing that PMDsc-R74H became dominant after serial dilution and regrowth under fosmidomycin selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.84</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="GROWTH-RATE EVIDENCE UNDER HIGH EXPRESSION">
  <data key="d0">GROWTH-RATE EVIDENCE UNDER HIGH EXPRESSION</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Observed similar growth rates of DH1 strains expressing active PMDsc K22M, R74H, and WT under 100 nM aTc, approximately 0.83 ± 0.01 h−1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ISOPENTENOL TITER EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">ISOPENTENOL TITER EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Production measurements showing that DH1 strains expressing M212Q, R74S, or I145A PMDsc mutants reached 600–800 mg/L isopentenol versus 475.1 mg/L for WT.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE SER208">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC ACTIVE-SITE SER208</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Serine 208 in Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphomevalonate decarboxylase; predicted to form essential hydrogen bonds with the alpha-phosphate of ATP and the alpha-phosphate of MVAPP, and required for active PMDsc selection.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSE ARG193-EQUIVALENT PHOSPHATE-STABILIZING POSITION">
  <data key="d0">PMDSE ARG193-EQUIVALENT PHOSPHATE-STABILIZING POSITION</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Arg193 in PMDse is described as stabilizing the beta-phosphate of MVAPP; PMDsc Thr209 is structurally parallel to this position.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.55</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC S208E INACTIVE MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC S208E INACTIVE MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Glutamate substitution at Ser208 of PMDsc; reported to be inactive toward MVAP and used as an inactive control in the screening platform. | Inactive PMDsc variant used as an additional negative control to reconfirm impaired growth in the screening platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d7">PMDSC S155E INACTIVE MUTANT</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC S208A DESTABILIZING MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC S208A DESTABILIZING MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Alanine substitution at Ser208 of PMDsc; reported to compromise structural stability and cause protein precipitation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC T209D MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC T209D MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Aspartate substitution at Thr209 of PMDsc; previously shown not to significantly change isopentenol titer in E. coli.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.55</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC R74S MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC R74S MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Arg74-to-serine PMDsc substitution identified by screening; significantly improved isopentenol production through the IPP-bypass MVA pathway. | Arg74-to-histidine PMDsc substitution from a previous study; increased isopentenol production to about 770.3 mg/L.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.85</data>
  <data key="d7">PMDSC R74H MUTANT</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC I145A MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC I145A MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Ile145-to-alanine PMDsc substitution identified by screening; significantly improved isopentenol production through the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC M212Q MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC M212Q MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Met212-to-glutamine PMDsc substitution identified by screening; significantly improved isopentenol production through the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC DOUBLE MUTANTS R74S-I145A, R74S-M212Q, AND R74H-M212Q">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC DOUBLE MUTANTS R74S-I145A, R74S-M212Q, AND R74H-M212Q</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Selected PMDsc double-mutant combinations that further increased isopentenol titers up to 2.4-fold relative to wild type, reaching approximately 900–1130 mg/L after 48 h induction.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC ACTIVITY TOWARD NONNATIVE MVAP">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC ACTIVITY TOWARD NONNATIVE MVAP</data>
  <data key="d1">SELECTIVITY_PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d2">Functional preference or promiscuous activity of PMDsc toward mevalonate monophosphate, the nonnative substrate in the IPP-bypass MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC DECARBOXYLATION OF MVAP">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC DECARBOXYLATION OF MVAP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Decarboxylation reaction catalyzed by PMDsc on nonnative MVAP, enabling carbon flux through the IPP-bypass pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ATP AND MVAPP ALPHA-PHOSPHATE BINDING CONTACTS">
  <data key="d0">ATP AND MVAPP ALPHA-PHOSPHATE BINDING CONTACTS</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Predicted phosphate-binding contact network involving PMDsc Ser208 hydrogen bonds to the alpha-phosphate of ATP and the alpha-phosphate of MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE STABILIZATION SITE">
  <data key="d0">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE STABILIZATION SITE</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Phosphate-stabilizing site associated with the PMDse Arg193-equivalent position, proposed to stabilize the beta-phosphate of MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.55</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="SCREENING PLATFORM FOR ACTIVE PMDSC VARIANTS">
  <data key="d0">SCREENING PLATFORM FOR ACTIVE PMDSC VARIANTS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth-coupled screening platform using PMDsc activity toward MVAP to select active variants and identify mutations increasing carbon flux and isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ISOPENTENOL TITER INCREASE">
  <data key="d0">ISOPENTENOL TITER INCREASE</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Production output used to evaluate PMDsc variants: wild type produced about 475.1 mg/L, single mutants reached about 600–800 mg/L, and selected double mutants reached about 900–1130 mg/L.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="RELATIVE GROWTH RATE UNDER SCREENING CONDITIONS">
  <data key="d0">RELATIVE GROWTH RATE UNDER SCREENING CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth phenotype used as a proxy for PMDsc-dependent carbon flux through the IPP-bypass pathway in the screening platform.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.65</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="CODON SATURATION MUTAGENESIS LIBRARY EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">CODON SATURATION MUTAGENESIS LIBRARY EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Seven codon saturation mutagenesis libraries demonstrated that the platform could identify PMDsc mutants with potentially higher activity toward MVAP and increased isopentenol titers.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="STRUCTURAL PREDICTION EVIDENCE FOR SER208 CONTACTS">
  <data key="d0">STRUCTURAL PREDICTION EVIDENCE FOR SER208 CONTACTS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Alignment-based structural prediction mapping PMDsc onto a PMDse crystal structure supports a role for Ser208 in ATP and MVAPP alpha-phosphate binding.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_5</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC ENZYME SCAFFOLD">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC ENZYME SCAFFOLD</data>
  <data key="d1">DOMAIN</data>
  <data key="d2">Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphomevalonate decarboxylase variant scaffold used for engineering isopentenol production through the IPP-bypass route; WT PMDsc produced 475.1 mg/L isopentenol after 48 h induction.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ENGINEERED IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY">
  <data key="d0">ENGINEERED IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Metabolic-engineering context in DH1 strains carrying JBEI-9310 where PMDsc variants convert MVAP in an IPP-bypass route to support isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.92</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAP DECARBOXYLATION">
  <data key="d0">MVAP DECARBOXYLATION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc-catalyzed decarboxylation of mevalonate-5-phosphate; inferred from growth-rate/titer coupling to be the rate-limiting step in the engineered IPP-bypass pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">1.0</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAP-ASSOCIATED POCKET GEOMETRY">
  <data key="d0">MVAP-ASSOCIATED POCKET GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Substrate-proximal structural environment around MVAP in PMDsc, represented with helices H1, H2, H4, and H5 and the identified mutational residues.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.76</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC HELICES H1-H2-H4-H5">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC HELICES H1-H2-H4-H5</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Secondary-structure elements shown near MVAP: α-helix 1/H1, α-helix 2/H2, and α-helices 4-5/H4-H5, which spatially frame residues identified by mutagenesis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="IDENTIFIED PMDSC RESIDUE POSITIONS">
  <data key="d0">IDENTIFIED PMDSC RESIDUE POSITIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">RESIDUE</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutationally identified PMDsc positions affecting isopentenol production and/or catalytic properties, including Y19, K22, R74, Q140, E144/I145, R147, S186, Q210/M212, I226, and V230.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.88</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74H-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">R74H-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">High-producing PMDsc triple variant with 48 h isopentenol titer of about 1079-1080 mg/L, growth rate 0.79 h^-1, kcat 0.16 s^-1, KM 0.4 mM, and kcat/KM 0.4 mM^-1 s^-1. | PMDsc triple variant with very low 48 h isopentenol titer of 8 mg/L; growth rate was not determined, indicating that combining individually promising substitutions can be deleterious.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.98</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.98</data>
  <data key="d7">R74G-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE MUTANT</data>
</node>
<node id="R74G-R147K DOUBLE MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">R74G-R147K DOUBLE MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc double variant with high cellular growth and production: growth rate 0.84 h^-1 and 48 h isopentenol titer 909 mg/L; kcat/KM was 0.42 mM^-1 s^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74G SINGLE MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">R74G SINGLE MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc single variant with high isopentenol titer of 975 mg/L and growth rate 0.81 h^-1, despite relatively low measured catalytic efficiency of 0.04 mM^-1 s^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="K22Y SINGLE MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">K22Y SINGLE MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Low-producing PMDsc single variant that defined the lower end of the selected mutant range, producing 22 ± 8 mg/L isopentenol with growth rate 0.13 h^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.74</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="MICHAELIS CONSTANT KM">
  <data key="d0">MICHAELIS CONSTANT KM</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Apparent substrate affinity parameter for MVAP; WT KM was 2.3 mM, while several improved variants showed lower KM values such as 0.35-0.75 mM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.78</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="CATALYTIC EFFICIENCY KCAT/KM">
  <data key="d0">CATALYTIC EFFICIENCY KCAT/KM</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Composite in vitro catalytic efficiency metric for PMDsc variants; WT was 0.066 mM^-1 s^-1, while selected mutants reached approximately 0.4-0.78 mM^-1 s^-1.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="CELLULAR GROWTH RATE">
  <data key="d0">CELLULAR GROWTH RATE</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Growth-rate phenotype measured in h^-1 for mutant strains; it correlated positively with isopentenol titer and was used as an indicator of pathway flux through MVAP decarboxylation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7,8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="GROWTH-RATE VERSUS TITER CORRELATION EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">GROWTH-RATE VERSUS TITER CORRELATION EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Scatter plot of 20 selected mutants showing a positive linear correlation between cellular growth rate and isopentenol titer with R^2 = 0.72; correlation was stronger among the eight high producers.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.93</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="RANDOM MUTAGENESIS SCREENING EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">RANDOM MUTAGENESIS SCREENING EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Screening of random mutagenesis libraries in DH1 strains containing JBEI-9310, followed by single and triple mutant construction; titers were calculated from three biological replicates after 24 h and 48 h induction.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="KINETIC AND PRODUCTION TABLE EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d0">KINETIC AND PRODUCTION TABLE EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Table of WT and selected PMDsc mutants reporting kcat, KM, kcat/KM, growth rate, and 48 h titer, enabling comparison between in vitro kinetics and cellular production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.91</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_7</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ARG74 SUBSTITUTIONS">
  <data key="d0">ARG74 SUBSTITUTIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutational variants at position 74, especially R74H, R74G, and R74S, that improve production phenotypes; the benefit of glycine and serine indicates that a protonated side chain at this site is not required. | Single mutant whose kcat/KM is comparable to wild type but whose expressing strain produced significantly more isopentenol than wild type.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d7">R74G SUBSTITUTION</data>
</node>
<node id="ILE145 SUBSTITUTIONS">
  <data key="d0">ILE145 SUBSTITUTIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Variants at position 145, including I145F and I145A, associated with modestly improved PMDsc activity or enhanced screening outcomes, suggesting that side-chain packing near this position influences activity.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="NEIGHBORING ALPHA-HELIX PACKING">
  <data key="d0">NEIGHBORING ALPHA-HELIX PACKING</data>
  <data key="d1">POCKET_GEOMETRY</data>
  <data key="d2">Altered packing modes between neighboring alpha helices proposed to transmit the effects of distal substitutions such as Arg74 and Ile145 to PMDsc catalytic behavior.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.82</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="SUBSTRATE-BINDING LOOP RESIDUES 17-33">
  <data key="d0">SUBSTRATE-BINDING LOOP RESIDUES 17-33</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">A loop containing several substrate-binding domain residues proposed to be critical for catalysis; Arg74 is described as interacting with this loop.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.86</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="H2 ALPHA HELIX">
  <data key="d0">H2 ALPHA HELIX</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">An alpha-helical segment of PMDsc whose C-terminal end contains Ser120 and Ser121, residues implicated in stabilizing MVAP with ATP. | Alpha helix 4 of PMDsc, containing distant residues Gln210, Ile226, and Val230 that may influence MVAP substrate-binding modes.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.72</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.72</data>
  <data key="d7">H4 ALPHA HELIX</data>
</node>
<node id="SER120-SER121 MOTIF">
  <data key="d0">SER120-SER121 MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d1">MOTIF</data>
  <data key="d2">Two serine residues at the C-terminal end of H2 that provide essential hydrogen bonds stabilizing MVAP with ATP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.83</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
