<node id="Y19H SUBSTITUTION">
  <data key="d0">Y19H SUBSTITUTION</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Mutation of Tyr19 to histidine; produced the largest reported increase in kcat/KM relative to wild type but significantly decreased isopentenol titer.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74G-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE SUBSTITUTION">
  <data key="d0">R74G-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE SUBSTITUTION</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Triple mutant with kcat/KM comparable to R74H-R147K-M212Q but much lower isopentenol titer after 48 hours. | Triple mutant with kcat/KM comparable to R74G-R147K-M212Q but substantially higher isopentenol titer after 48 hours.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.8</data>
  <data key="d7">R74H-R147K-M212Q TRIPLE SUBSTITUTION</data>
</node>
<node id="KINETIC-PHENOTYPE NON-CORRELATION">
  <data key="d0">KINETIC-PHENOTYPE NON-CORRELATION</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Correlation analysis showing no significant relationship between kcat or kcat/KM and either cellular growth rate or isopentenol titer across characterized PMDsc mutants.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="TABLE 2 MEASUREMENTS">
  <data key="d0">TABLE 2 MEASUREMENTS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Reported kinetic parameters and production data for PMDsc variants, including M212Q, Y19H, R74G, and triple mutants. | Reported substrate-inhibition constants for selected PMDsc variants, supporting the association between higher KI and higher isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.85</data>
  <data key="d7">TABLE 3 KI MEASUREMENTS</data>
</node>
<node id="SUPPLEMENTARY FIG. S7 CORRELATION ANALYSIS">
  <data key="d0">SUPPLEMENTARY FIG. S7 CORRELATION ANALYSIS</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Figure supporting the conclusion that mutant kinetic activity is not significantly correlated with isopentenol titer or cellular growth rate.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="STRUCTURAL ALIGNMENT MODEL">
  <data key="d0">STRUCTURAL ALIGNMENT MODEL</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Model used to infer proximity of Met212 to the predicted alpha-phosphate binding site of MVAP.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PRIOR COMPUTATIONAL STUDY ON RESIDUE 19">
  <data key="d0">PRIOR COMPUTATIONAL STUDY ON RESIDUE 19</data>
  <data key="d1">EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d2">Previous computational analysis suggesting that mutations at residue 19 might improve alpha-phosphate stabilization.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.7</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_9</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION">
  <data key="d0">PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Decarboxylation of mevalonate-5-phosphate (MVAP) by Saccharomyces cerevisiae phosphomevalonate decarboxylase (PMDsc) to produce isopentenyl phosphate-related product flux in the IPP-bypass mevalonate pathway.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="NONCOMPETITIVE SUBSTRATE INHIBITION BY MVAP">
  <data key="d0">NONCOMPETITIVE SUBSTRATE INHIBITION BY MVAP</data>
  <data key="d1">DYNAMICAL_STATE</data>
  <data key="d2">Inhibitory kinetic regime in which excess MVAP decreases PMDsc decarboxylation activity; characterized by the substrate inhibition constant KI.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="HIGH IN VIVO MVAP ACCUMULATION">
  <data key="d0">HIGH IN VIVO MVAP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">Production strains containing the IPP-bypass mevalonate pathway and wild-type PMD accumulated high MVAP concentrations after induction, potentially well above the KM of PMDsc.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION AND GROWTH-SELECTION CONDITIONS">
  <data key="d0">ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION AND GROWTH-SELECTION CONDITIONS</data>
  <data key="d1">CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d2">In vivo engineering context in E. coli where PMDsc mutant performance is assessed by isopentenol titers and growth behavior under pathway-selection conditions.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.9</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="WT PMDSC">
  <data key="d0">WT PMDSC</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Wild-type PMDsc used as the reference enzyme variant; reported to have KM(MVAP) = 2.3 ± 0.2 mM and KI = 18 mM under MVAP substrate-inhibition analysis.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74G PMDSC MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">R74G PMDSC MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc variant carrying the R74G substitution; produced significantly higher isopentenol than WT and showed elevated substrate-inhibition resistance with KI = 110 mM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="V230E PMDSC MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">V230E PMDSC MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">PMDsc variant carrying the V230E substitution; included in the substrate-inhibition study and showed relatively low KI = 10 mM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="R74G-R147K-M212Q PMDSC MUTANT">
  <data key="d0">R74G-R147K-M212Q PMDSC MUTANT</data>
  <data key="d1">SEQUENCE_FEATURE</data>
  <data key="d2">Triple PMDsc mutant containing R74G, R147K, and M212Q substitutions; included in the substrate-inhibition study and showed low KI = 11 mM despite containing R74G. | Triple PMDsc mutant containing R74H, R147K, and M212Q substitutions; a higher isopentenol-producing mutant with elevated KI = 80 mM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.8</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
  <data key="d6">0.9</data>
  <data key="d7">R74H-R147K-M212Q PMDSC MUTANT</data>
</node>
<node id="MVAP INHIBITION CONSTANT KI">
  <data key="d0">MVAP INHIBITION CONSTANT KI</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Noncompetitive substrate-inhibition constant for MVAP; higher KI indicates reduced sensitivity to inhibition at high MVAP concentrations. Reported values include WT 18 mM, R74G 110 mM, V230E 10 mM, R74G-R147K-M212Q 11 mM, and R74H-R147K-M212Q 80 mM.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.98</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="KM FOR MVAP">
  <data key="d0">KM FOR MVAP</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Michaelis constant for MVAP binding/turnover by PMDsc; WT PMDsc has KM(MVAP) = 2.3 ± 0.2 mM, making high intracellular MVAP potentially inhibitory rather than simply saturating.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="KCAT AND KCAT/KM FOR PMDSC MUTANTS">
  <data key="d0">KCAT AND KCAT/KM FOR PMDSC MUTANTS</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">In vitro catalytic turnover and catalytic-efficiency metrics for PMDsc mutants. The text notes that increases in these values alone did not fully explain in vivo isopentenol titers.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.85</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="OBSERVED TURNOVER NUMBER KOBS AT 100 MM MVAP">
  <data key="d0">OBSERVED TURNOVER NUMBER KOBS AT 100 MM MVAP</data>
  <data key="d1">KINETIC_PARAMETER</data>
  <data key="d2">Calculated apparent turnover number under high-MVAP conditions using the analytical expression for noncompetitive substrate inhibition; depends on each mutant's kcat, KM, and KI.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.95</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</node>
<node id="PMK-DIRECTED MVAP FLUX TO MVAPP">
  <data key="d0">PMK-DIRECTED MVAP FLUX TO MVAPP</data>
  <data key="d1">REACTION_STEP</data>
  <data key="d2">Competing pathway step in which phosphomevalonate kinase converts MVAP to MVAPP, the preferred native substrate for PMDsc, rather than allowing futile MVAP decarboxylation.</data>
  <data key="d3">0.75</data>
  <data key="d4">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d5">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
