  <data key="d9">ATPΓS TRIPHOSPHORYL POSITIONING</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Near-wild-type KM in the S192A mutant supports the interpretation that Ser192 contributes to phosphoryl positioning and catalysis rather than substrate binding.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.68</data>
  <data key="d13">3</data>
  <data key="d14">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_5</data>
