  <data key="d8">WT MDD TERNARY FMVAPP-ATPΓS CRYSTALLIZATION CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d9">ABSENCE OF STABLY COORDINATED MG2+</data>
  <data key="d10">CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d11">The absence of Mg2+ was observed specifically in the ternary FMVAPP-ATPγS wild-type MDD crystallization context.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.72</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_6</data>
  <data key="d15">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ABSENCE OF STABLY COORDINATED MG2+" target="NO MG2+ ELECTRON-DENSITY EVIDENCE">
  <data key="d8">ABSENCE OF STABLY COORDINATED MG2+</data>
  <data key="d9">NO MG2+ ELECTRON-DENSITY EVIDENCE</data>
  <data key="d10">SUPPORTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d11">The claim that Mg2+ is absent from the ternary complex is supported by the lack of interpretable electron density for a coordinated Mg2+ atom.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.94</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_6</data>
  <data key="d15">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ABSENCE OF STABLY COORDINATED MG2+" target="FMVAPP C3-HYDROXYL TO ATPΓS Γ-PHOSPHORYL SEPARATION">
  <data key="d8">ABSENCE OF STABLY COORDINATED MG2+</data>
  <data key="d9">FMVAPP C3-HYDROXYL TO ATPΓS Γ-PHOSPHORYL SEPARATION</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">The lack of coordinated Mg2+ may explain the relatively large 5.5 Å separation between the substrate-analogue hydroxyl and nucleotide γ-phosphoryl group.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.86</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257_chunk_6</data>
  <data key="d15">a9c7009e-9e90-565c-abe8-c021976be257</data>
</edge>
