  <data key="d9">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">IPP accumulation is one specific toxic intermediate accumulation state within the engineered MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.75</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP ACCUMULATION" target="IPP-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION">
  <data key="d8">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Accumulation of IPP is described as inhibiting cell growth and preventing sufficient biomass formation.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.91</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP ACCUMULATION" target="STRESS RESPONSES FROM PRENYL DIPHOSPHATE ACCUMULATION">
  <data key="d8">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d9">STRESS RESPONSES FROM PRENYL DIPHOSPHATE ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d10">ALLOWS</data>
  <data key="d11">Transient IPP accumulation is proposed to induce stress responses, analogous to observations with FPP accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.7</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP ACCUMULATION" target="IPP TOXICITY AND GROWTH INHIBITION">
  <data key="d8">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP TOXICITY AND GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">High IPP accumulation is linked to growth inhibition, indicating that IPP is toxic relative to IP.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.91</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION" target="ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">IPP-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d9">ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Growth inhibition limits biomass accumulation and therefore constrains achievable isopentenol titer.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.82</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
