<edge source="STRESS RESPONSES FROM PRENYL DIPHOSPHATE ACCUMULATION" target="ATP-DEPENDENT DEFENSE MECHANISMS">
  <data key="d8">STRESS RESPONSES FROM PRENYL DIPHOSPHATE ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d9">ATP-DEPENDENT DEFENSE MECHANISMS</data>
  <data key="d10">COUPLES_TO</data>
  <data key="d11">Generalized and condition-specific stress responses recruit ATP-consuming mechanisms such as DNA repair, ATPases, and ABC transporters.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.78</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ATP-DEPENDENT DEFENSE MECHANISMS" target="ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">ATP-DEPENDENT DEFENSE MECHANISMS</data>
  <data key="d9">ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">ATP consumed by stress-defense processes may compete with the energetically expensive MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.75</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
