<edge source="ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY" target="ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d9">ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Energetic competition and ATP costs can reduce yield and productivity of isopentenol production.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NATIVE IPP ISOMERASE DIVERSION" target="GPP AND FPP FORMATION">
  <data key="d8">NATIVE IPP ISOMERASE DIVERSION</data>
  <data key="d9">GPP AND FPP FORMATION</data>
  <data key="d10">MEDIATES</data>
  <data key="d11">Native E. coli IPP isomerase Idi diverts IPP into pathways that generate GPP and FPP.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.86</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="GPP AND FPP FORMATION" target="CARBON UTILIZATION EFFICIENCY OF ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">GPP AND FPP FORMATION</data>
  <data key="d9">CARBON UTILIZATION EFFICIENCY OF ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Formation of GPP and FPP diverts carbon away from isopentenol, decreasing carbon utilization efficiency.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.84</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="GPP AND FPP FORMATION" target="PMD ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d8">GPP AND FPP FORMATION</data>
  <data key="d9">MK ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">GPP and FPP potentially inhibit mevalonate kinase activity, which can reduce downstream MVA flux.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.7</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-DEPENDENT DIPHOSPHATE FORMATION AND HYDROLYSIS" target="ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">IPP-DEPENDENT DIPHOSPHATE FORMATION AND HYDROLYSIS</data>
  <data key="d9">ENERGETIC BURDEN OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">ATP-consuming diphosphate formation followed by hydrolysis is inefficient in atom and energy economy.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.88</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY" target="IPP ACCUMULATION">
  <data key="d8">IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d10">ALLOWS</data>
  <data key="d11">An IPP-dependent design creates conditions where high pathway flux can cause IPP buildup.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.86</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY" target="ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d9">ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Dependence on IPP intrinsically limits engineering of more efficient isopentenol production because of toxicity, carbon diversion, and energy inefficiency.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS" target="MVA OR MVA PHOSPHATE DECARBOXYLATION TO ISOPENTENOL">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS</data>
  <data key="d9">MVA OR MVA PHOSPHATE DECARBOXYLATION TO ISOPENTENOL</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">The IPP-bypass designs rely on decarboxylation of MVA or MVA phosphate to generate isopentenol.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.92</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS" target="IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP DEPENDENCY OF THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">The bypass pathways decouple isopentenol production from IPP and therefore reduce dependence on IPP formation.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS" target="IPP ACCUMULATION">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Because IPP is no longer required as the essential precursor, the bypass pathways are designed to eliminate negative effects of IPP accumulation.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.89</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS" target="ORIGINAL MVA-TO-ISOPENTENOL PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY I</data>
  <data key="d9">ORIGINAL MVA-TO-ISOPENTENOL PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">SHIFTS</data>
  <data key="d11">Pathway I shifts isopentenol production away from the canonical IPP-forming route by bypassing IPP and reducing ATP use from three to one. | Pathway II shifts isopentenol production away from the canonical IPP-forming route by replacing IPP with IP and reducing ATP use from three to two.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_4</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
