  <data key="d9">MVAP ACCUMULATION</data>
  <data key="d10">ALLOWS</data>
  <data key="d11">Pathway II accumulates MVAP instead of IPP, with MVAP levels reported to be approximately 100–200 mM.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.87</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAYS" target="IPP TOXICITY AND GROWTH INHIBITION">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY II</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP TOXICITY AND GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Because pathway II does not produce IPP, it is expected to be free from IPP-related toxicity and less sensitive to MK-expression changes.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.89</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_10</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
