  <data key="d8">PMDHV LACK OF MVAPP ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDHV MVAP-SPECIFIC SELECTIVITY PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">Absence of MVAPP activity is part of the selectivity profile that makes PMDhv MVAP-specific.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.86</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="NO ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION IN ARK5" target="PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE">
  <data key="d8">NO ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION IN ARK5</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE</data>
  <data key="d10">SUPPORTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d11">Failure to detect isopentenol in vivo supports the interpretation that PMDhv did not function effectively in E. coli.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.87</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ATP-NADH COUPLED MVAP ASSAY FOR PMDHV" target="PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE">
  <data key="d8">ATP-NADH COUPLED MVAP ASSAY FOR PMDHV</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE</data>
  <data key="d10">SUPPORTED_BY</data>
  <data key="d11">The absence of ATP hydrolysis in vitro supports the proposed inactive state of PMDhv under the tested non-native conditions.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.86</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE" target="IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY II WITH PMDHV IN E. COLI">
  <data key="d8">PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP-BYPASS PATHWAY II WITH PMDHV IN E. COLI</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">PMDhv inactivity in E. coli constrains its ability to support the engineered bypass pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.88</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE" target="H. VOLCANII NATIVE HIGH-SALT 42C EXPRESSION CONTEXT">
  <data key="d8">PMDHV INACTIVE-IN-E. COLI STATE</data>
  <data key="d9">H. VOLCANII NATIVE HIGH-SALT 42C EXPRESSION CONTEXT</data>
  <data key="d10">CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d11">The proposed inactivity in E. coli is interpreted in light of PMDhv being characterized previously under native high-salt, high-temperature H. volcanii conditions.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.82</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC POSITIVELY CHARGED ARGININE NEAR MVAP SITE" target="PMDSC MVAP PROMISCUOUS ACTIVITY PROFILE">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC POSITIVELY CHARGED ARGININE NEAR MVAP SITE</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDSC MVAP PROMISCUITY PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d10">ALLOWS</data>
  <data key="d11">The positively charged arginine is proposed to permit PMDsc promiscuity toward the less negatively charged MVAP substrate.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.74</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC PHOSPHATE-BINDING INSERTION RESIDUES ABSENT FROM PMDHV" target="PMDHV LACK OF MVAPP ACTIVITY">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC PHOSPHATE-BINDING INSERTION RESIDUES ABSENT FROM PMDHV</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDHV LACK OF MVAPP ACTIVITY</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Loss of PMDsc-like phosphate-binding residues in PMDhv provides a structural rationale for PMDhv lacking MVAPP activity.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SERINE/ARGININE-RICH PMD PHOSPHATE-BINDING SEGMENT" target="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT">
  <data key="d8">SERINE/ARGININE-RICH PMD PHOSPHATE-BINDING SEGMENT</data>
  <data key="d9">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT</data>
  <data key="d10">MEDIATES</data>
  <data key="d11">Serine- and arginine-rich residues facilitate interactions with phosphoryl moieties of MVAPP and ATP in the phosphate-proximal active-site environment.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.83</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT" target="PMDSC MVAP PROMISCUOUS ACTIVITY PROFILE">
  <data key="d8">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT</data>
  <data key="d9">PMDSC MVAP PROMISCUITY PROFILE</data>
  <data key="d10">DETERMINES</data>
  <data key="d11">The local electrostatic environment near the phosphate-binding site is proposed to determine how well PMDsc accepts MVAP.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.87</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC K22 S155 S208 T209 PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL SITE" target="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC K22 S155 S208 T209 PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL SITE</data>
  <data key="d9">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT</data>
  <data key="d10">LOCALIZES_TO</data>
  <data key="d11">K22, S155, S208, and T209 are positioned near the MVAPP phosphate region and define a local electrostatic redesign site.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.92</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="SUBSTRATE CHARGE GRADIENT MVAPP MVAP MVA" target="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT">
  <data key="d8">SUBSTRATE CHARGE GRADIENT MVAPP MVAP MVA</data>
  <data key="d9">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">The reduced negative charge of MVAP and MVA relative to MVAPP constrains how the phosphate-proximal pocket should be redesigned.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.91</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC CHARGE-COMPENSATING MUTATIONS K22M S155E S208E T209D" target="MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC CHARGE-COMPENSATING MUTATIONS K22M S155E S208E T209D</data>
  <data key="d9">MVAPP BETA-PHOSPHATE-PROXIMAL ELECTROSTATIC ENVIRONMENT</data>
  <data key="d10">SHIFTS</data>
  <data key="d11">The designed mutations alter the local electrostatic environment by reducing positive charge or introducing negative charge near the phosphate moiety.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC CHARGE-COMPENSATING MUTATIONS K22M S155E S208E T209D" target="SUBSTRATE CHARGE GRADIENT MVAPP MVAP MVA">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC CHARGE-COMPENSATING MUTATIONS K22M S155E S208E T209D</data>
  <data key="d9">SUBSTRATE CHARGE GRADIENT MVAPP MVAP MVA</data>
  <data key="d10">CONTEXT_DEPENDENT_ON</data>
  <data key="d11">The rationale for the mutations depends on the lower net negative charges of MVAP and MVA compared with MVAPP.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.85</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
  <data key="d15">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC R74H AND I145F MUTATIONS" target="3-HMB-TO-ISOBUTENE DECARBOXYLATION">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC R74H AND I145F MUTATIONS</data>
  <data key="d9">3-HMB-TO-ISOBUTENE DECARBOXYLATION</data>
  <data key="d10">SHIFTS</data>
  <data key="d11">R74H and I145F were selected because they had previously increased PMDsc activity in the related 3-HMB-to-isobutene decarboxylation reaction.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.72</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">dd599823-57fe-59b5-bf71-6ef7c22b4a8a_chunk_8</data>
