<edge source="IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION" target="IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">By bypassing IPP dependency, the alternative pathway is designed to reduce limitations associated with IPP accumulation and toxicity.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION" target="ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d9">ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">The bypass design addresses the high ATP burden associated with generating IPP through the conventional MVA pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.75</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION" target="IPP-BYPASS SCREENING PLATFORM">
  <data key="d8">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP-BYPASS SCREENING PLATFORM</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">The screening platform includes the five reactions of the IPP-bypass isopentenol pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY" target="CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d9">CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">IPP generation is a core step of the conventional MVA-based isopentenol production route. | The requirement for three ATP molecules per IPP imposes an energetic constraint on the conventional pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION" target="CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d9">CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">Hydrolysis of IPP to produce isopentenol is part of the conventional IPP-dependent production route.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.85</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION" target="ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY">
  <data key="d8">IPP DIPHOSPHATE HYDROLYSIS IN CONVENTIONAL ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d9">ATP-CONSUMING IPP GENERATION THROUGH THE MVA PATHWAY</data>
  <data key="d10">EXPLAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Hydrolysis of the IPP diphosphate group explains why ATP invested during IPP formation is squandered in the conventional isopentenol route.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION" target="CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">IPP ACCUMULATION-ASSOCIATED GROWTH INHIBITION</data>
  <data key="d9">CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">CONSTRAINS</data>
  <data key="d11">Potential toxicity from IPP accumulation makes engineering of the conventional IPP-dependent pathway more complicated and inefficient.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.9</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="OPTIMAL INTRACELLULAR IPP LEVEL" target="CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">OPTIMAL INTRACELLULAR IPP LEVEL</data>
  <data key="d9">CONVENTIONAL IPP-DEPENDENT MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">GATES</data>
  <data key="d11">Efficient production in the conventional pathway depends on maintaining IPP high enough for flux but low enough to avoid growth inhibition.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.8</data>
  <data key="d13">2</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
<edge source="PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION TO IP" target="IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION">
  <data key="d8">PMDSC-CATALYZED MVAP DECARBOXYLATION TO IP</data>
  <data key="d9">IPP-BYPASS MVA PATHWAY FOR ISOPENTENOL PRODUCTION</data>
  <data key="d10">PART_OF</data>
  <data key="d11">Promiscuous decarboxylation of MVAP to IP by PMDsc is a defining reaction of the IPP-bypass pathway.</data>
  <data key="d12">0.95</data>
  <data key="d13">1</data>
  <data key="d14">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294_chunk_1</data>
  <data key="d15">8b12a598-340d-5340-aebf-b31ea016d294</data>
</edge>
